 <p id="source-aim2b">The PAPI indications are depicted only in AIM FIG 2-1-5, an image; the angles given with Figure 7 are from that figure as commonly reproduced and have not been checked against text.</p>
 <p id="source-aim4"><strong>[2] FAA, AIM, Chapter 4, Section 3, Airport Operations:</strong> <a href="https://www.faa.gov/air_traffic/publications/atpubs/aim_html/chap4_section_3.html">faa.gov</a>. Inspected 25 October 2026: ¶4-3-2, 4-3-3, 4-3-4, 4-3-6, 4-3-13 (light signal table), 4-3-18 and 4-3-21.</p>
 <p id="source-pcg"><strong>[3] FAA, Pilot/Controller Glossary:</strong> <a href="https://www.faa.gov/air_traffic/publications/atpubs/pcg_html/glossary-o.html">"Overhead maneuver" (O)</a>; <a href="https://www.faa.gov/air_traffic/publications/atpubs/pcg_html/glossary-t.html">"Threshold", "Traffic pattern" and "Tetrahedron" (T)</a> (faa.gov). Inspected 25 October 2026.</p>
 <p id="source-afh"><strong>[4] FAA, Airplane Flying Handbook (FAA-H-8083-3C), Chapter 8, Airport Traffic Patterns:</strong> <a href="https://www.faa.gov/sites/faa.gov/files/regulations_policies/handbooks_manuals/aviation/airplane_handbook/09_afh_ch8.pdf">PDF (faa.gov)</a>, pp. 8-1 to 8-4. Inspected 25 October 2026.</p>
 <p id="source-ac"><strong>[5] FAA, Advisory Circular AC 90-66C, Non-Towered Airport Flight Operations, 6 June 2023:</strong> <a href="https://www.faa.gov/documentlibrary/media/advisory_circular/ac_90-66c.pdf">PDF (faa.gov)</a>, ¶9.11.1, 11.3 and 11.8. Inspected 25 October 2026.</p>
 <p id="source-atc"><strong>[6] FAA Order JO 7110.65, Air Traffic Control, ¶3-10-12, Overhead Maneuver:</strong> <a href="https://www.faa.gov/air_traffic/publications/atpubs/atc_html/chap3_section_10.html">faa.gov</a>. Inspected 25 October 2026.</p>
 <p>Page-specific excerpts are recorded in the repository review evidence: <a href="https://github.com/burnzoire/oversweep/blob/main/docs/reviews/airfield-ops-faa-evidence.md">FAA airfield evidence</a>.</p>
 <p>Figures 1–11 are original line drawings, not reproductions of any FAA figure, and are not to scale except where a caption says so. The wind, PAPI and overhead figures use the simple models described with them.</p>
 <p class="note">Applicability: US (FAA) standards for civil airports, as published online on the inspection date. ICAO states and military airfields differ in detail, and every airfield's own published procedures take precedence. This revision is Drafted pending independent source-backed review.</p>
